<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>The agent band - Harness</title>
  <meta name="description" content="A live, simulated preview of the agent band: a mod that sits above the Claude Code prompt and shows limits, context, cost and every agent.">
  <script>
    try {
      const savedTheme = localStorage.getItem("harness-map-theme");
      const prefersDark = window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches;
      if (savedTheme === "dark" || (savedTheme === null && prefersDark)) document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "dark";
    } catch (error) {
      console.warn("The saved theme could not be read.", error);
    }
  </script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css?v={{style_hash}}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="band.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <div class="page-title-row">
        <h1 class="page-title">The agent band</h1>
        <button type="button" class="theme-switch" role="switch" aria-checked="false" data-theme-toggle>
          <span class="theme-switch-track" aria-hidden="true"><span class="theme-switch-thumb"></span></span>
          <span class="theme-switch-label">Dark</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <p class="page-lede">A strip above the Claude Code prompt that shows your limits, your context, what the session costs and what every agent is doing right now. It is a separate plugin and works with or without the harness.</p>
      <p><a href="index.html">&larr; Back to the Harness Map</a></p>
    </header>

    <main class="bp-main">
      <section class="bp-preview" aria-labelledby="preview-title">
        <div class="bp-toolbar">
          <h2 class="bp-title" id="preview-title">Live preview</h2>
          <div class="bp-controls">
            <div class="install-tablist" role="group" aria-label="Billing">
              <button type="button" class="install-tab install-mode" data-billing-choice="subscription" aria-pressed="true">Subscription</button>
              <button type="button" class="install-tab install-mode" data-billing-choice="api" aria-pressed="false">API</button>
            </div>
            <div class="install-tablist" role="group" aria-label="Band theme">
              <button type="button" class="install-tab install-mode" data-theme-choice="light" aria-pressed="true">Light</button>
              <button type="button" class="install-tab install-mode" data-theme-choice="dark" aria-pressed="false">Dark</button>
            </div>
            <button type="button" class="bp-pause" data-pause aria-pressed="false">Pause</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="bp-note">Simulated: agents start, think, run tools, finish or fail on a timer, six times faster than real. Press the chevron to fold the band, pick a range, or hover a tile for its facts.</p>

        <div class="band" data-band>
          <div class="fold" data-view="folded" hidden>
            <div class="fold-gauges">
              <svg class="ring" viewBox="0 0 26 26" role="img" aria-label="Limits and context rings" data-ring></svg>
              <div class="legend" data-legend></div>
            </div>
            <div class="fold-main">
              <div class="fold-main-line">
                <strong>main</strong>
                <span class="counts" data-counts>
                  <span class="count is-live" data-count="live"></span>
                  <span class="count is-done" data-count="done"></span>
                  <span class="count is-failed" data-count="failed"></span>
                </span>
              </div>
              <span class="activity" data-main-activity></span>
            </div>
            <svg class="lane" viewBox="0 0 112 16" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="Main and live agents over the last 5 minutes" data-lane></svg>
            <button type="button" class="fold-button" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Unfold the band" data-fold><span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          </div>

          <div class="open" data-view="open">
            <div class="gutter">
              <div class="gutter-limits" data-limits></div>
              <svg class="gutter-rule" viewBox="0 0 150 1" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="0" x2="150" y1="0.5" y2="0.5"/></svg>
              <dl class="spend" data-spend></dl>
            </div>
            <div class="open-main">
              <div class="open-head">
                <div class="ranges" role="group" aria-label="Range">
                  <button type="button" class="range" aria-pressed="false" data-range="1m">1m</button>
                  <button type="button" class="range" aria-pressed="true" data-range="5m">5m</button>
                  <button type="button" class="range" aria-pressed="false" data-range="1h">1h</button>
                  <button type="button" class="range" aria-pressed="false" data-range="all">all</button>
                </div>
                <span class="open-head-label">agents</span>
                <span class="counts" data-counts>
                  <span class="count is-live" data-count="live"></span>
                  <span class="count is-done" data-count="done"></span>
                  <span class="count is-failed" data-count="failed"></span>
                </span>
                <button type="button" class="fold-button" aria-expanded="true" aria-label="Fold the band" data-fold><span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
              </div>
              <ul class="tiles" data-tiles></ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="bp-lower">
        <section class="bp-read" aria-labelledby="read-title">
          <h2 class="bp-title" id="read-title">How to read it</h2>
          <ul class="bp-list">
            <li><strong>Rings.</strong> One ring per limit, outside in: <span class="key key-five">5 hour</span>, <span class="key key-week">week</span>, <span class="key key-fable">Fable</span> and <span class="key key-context">context</span>. Past 80% a number gains a warning mark; past 95% it turns red.</li>
            <li><strong>Folded.</strong> One row, two lines: limits and resets over context and cost, then the main session, its agent counts and a small timeline.</li>
            <li><strong>Unfolded.</strong> The left column lists each limit with its reset, then the session total, and the main session's and agents' estimated shares. The right shows a tile per agent.</li>
            <li><strong>A tile.</strong> Name, model, what it is doing now, a 24-cell strip of its recent activity, how long it ran, tokens in and out, and an estimated cost.</li>
            <li><strong>API billing.</strong> With no subscription limits there are no limit rings; the band shows context, tokens and cost instead.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="bp-install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
          <h2 class="bp-title" id="install-title">Install</h2>
          <div class="card install" data-install>
            <h3 class="install-title">The agent band</h3>
            <div class="install-bar">
              <div class="install-tablist" role="group" aria-label="Install or uninstall the band">
                <button type="button" class="install-tab install-mode" data-mode-choice="install" aria-pressed="true">Install</button>
                <button type="button" class="install-tab install-mode" data-mode-choice="uninstall" aria-pressed="false">Uninstall</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="install-panel">
              <code class="install-command" data-mode="install">[[@install-command band]]</code>
              <button type="button" class="install-copy" data-mode="install" data-copy="[[@install-copy band]]">Copy</button>
              <p class="install-note" data-mode="install">Run it again to update. Then restart Claude Code or run <code>/reload-plugins</code>. It runs in Claude Code only.</p>
              <code class="install-command" data-mode="uninstall" hidden>[[@install-command band-off]]</code>
              <button type="button" class="install-copy" data-mode="uninstall" hidden data-copy="[[@install-copy band-off]]">Copy</button>
              <p class="install-note" data-mode="uninstall" hidden>Restart Claude Code or run <code>/reload-plugins</code>. The harness plugin is not touched.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card install" data-install>
            <h3 class="install-title">The harness: agents, skills and hooks</h3>
            <div class="install-bar">
              <div class="install-tablist" role="group" aria-label="Install or uninstall the harness">
                <button type="button" class="install-tab install-mode" data-mode-choice="install" aria-pressed="true">Install</button>
                <button type="button" class="install-tab install-mode" data-mode-choice="uninstall" aria-pressed="false">Uninstall</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="install-panel">
              <code class="install-command" data-mode="install">[[@install-command claude]]</code>
              <button type="button" class="install-copy" data-mode="install" data-copy="[[@install-copy claude]]">Copy</button>
              <p class="install-note" data-mode="install">Needs <code>uv</code> on your <code>PATH</code>. Then restart Claude Code or run <code>/reload-plugins</code>, and <code>/harness:init</code> once per project. For Cortex Code and Kiro, see the <a href="index.html">Harness Map</a>.</p>
              <code class="install-command" data-mode="uninstall" hidden>[[@install-command claude-off]]</code>
              <button type="button" class="install-copy" data-mode="uninstall" hidden data-copy="[[@install-copy claude-off]]">Copy</button>
              <p class="install-note" data-mode="uninstall" hidden>Restart Claude Code or run <code>/reload-plugins</code>. The band plugin is not touched.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>

  <script defer src="band.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
